From ebbef91358246c860bee80f03393fa56de2810a6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ronny Stiftel <ronny.stiftel@tomcom.de>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 17:34:59 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Award covenant Blood Dregs from frozen native oath metadata

Use the original 1.09 native PvP reward calls and ItemLotParam rows: Corruption
awards one goods-704 Blood Dreg, while the original Radiance, Hunter and
blood-addled Hunter lots contain no item. Freeze normalized oath metadata at
match/join; mid-visit swaps cannot change the winner's entitlement.

Add the append-only covenant capability and validate the precise extended grant
shape. Legacy reward clients retain Insight/Echoes grants. Pending Dreg grants
remain whole and durable through old-client reconnects, and resume on a capable
login or capability upgrade. Document original asset checksums, native addresses,
field layouts and the 99-held/99-repository Blood Dreg capacity.

Validation: isolated opc ARM64 Docker image built successfully; all 10 focused
CTest suites passed, including frozen oath/empty-lot fixtures, both victory roles,
malformed goods, legacy shapes, solo durable reconnect and acknowledgement. No
production service, data, configuration or unrelated container was changed.
The client remains responsible for crash-atomic inventory/save delivery.

